# Convex Patterns

## Schema
- Schema lives in `convex/schema.ts` — single source of truth
- Every table has `orgId: v.string()` for multi-tenancy
- Every content table has `isDeleted: v.optional(v.boolean())`
- Dates are `v.number()` (Unix timestamps), never strings
- Use `v.optional()` for nullable fields
- **Money:** All monetary values stored as **integer cents** (e.g., $150.00 = 15000)

## Auth & Multi-Tenancy (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
- **Never** accept `orgId` as a client argument — always extract it server-side
- Use `ctx.auth.getUserIdentity()` → `identity.orgId` from the Clerk JWT
- Every query/mutation must validate authentication and extract `orgId` before any data access

## Query Pattern
```typescript
export const list = query({
  args: {},
  handler: async (ctx) => {
    const identity = await ctx.auth.getUserIdentity();
    if (!identity) throw new Error("Not authenticated");
    const orgId = identity.orgId as string;
    if (!orgId) throw new Error("No organization selected");

    return await ctx.db
      .query("tableName")
      .withIndex("by_orgId", (q) => q.eq("orgId", orgId))
      .filter((q) => q.neq(q.field("isDeleted"), true))
      .collect();
  },
});
```

## Mutation Pattern
```typescript
export const create = mutation({
  args: { name: v.string() },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    const identity = await ctx.auth.getUserIdentity();
    if (!identity) throw new Error("Not authenticated");
    const orgId = identity.orgId as string;
    if (!orgId) throw new Error("No organization selected");

    return await ctx.db.insert("tableName", {
      name: args.name,
      orgId,
      isDeleted: false,
    });
  },
});
```

## Soft Delete Pattern
```typescript
export const remove = mutation({
  args: { id: v.id("tableName") },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    const identity = await ctx.auth.getUserIdentity();
    if (!identity) throw new Error("Not authenticated");
    const orgId = identity.orgId as string;

    const doc = await ctx.db.get(args.id);
    if (!doc || doc.orgId !== orgId) throw new Error("Not found");

    await ctx.db.patch(args.id, { isDeleted: true });
  },
});
```

## Contact Search Pattern
Convex search indexes only support a single `searchField`. Contacts use a denormalized `searchText` field that concatenates searchable fields:

```typescript
// In create/update mutations, rebuild searchText:
const searchText = [company, firstName, lastName, email]
  .filter(Boolean)
  .join(" ");

await ctx.db.insert("contacts", { ...fields, searchText });

// In search queries:
export const search = query({
  args: { query: v.string() },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    const identity = await ctx.auth.getUserIdentity();
    if (!identity) throw new Error("Not authenticated");
    const orgId = identity.orgId as string;

    return await ctx.db
      .query("contacts")
      .withSearchIndex("search_contacts", (q) =>
        q.search("searchText", args.query).eq("orgId", orgId)
      )
      .filter((q) => q.neq(q.field("isDeleted"), true))
      .collect();
  },
});
```

## Indexes
- Define indexes for every query filter path in `schema.ts`
- Name convention: `by_fieldName` or `by_field1_and_field2`
- Compound indexes for multi-field queries

## Computed Billing State
Never store these — always compute in query handlers or helper functions:
```typescript
function computeNet(terms: PaymentTerms, scheduledPayments: ScheduledPayment[]): number {
  const lateFees = scheduledPayments
    .filter(sp => sp.dueDate < Date.now() && !sp.lateFeeWaived && !isFullyPaid(sp))
    .length * (terms.lateFeeType === "flat" ? (terms.lateFeeAmount ?? 0) : /* % calc */);

  const earlyDiscount = terms.earlyDiscountType === "flat"
    ? (terms.earlyDiscountAmount ?? 0)
    : Math.round(/* base * percent / 100 */);

  return terms.totalSale
    - (terms.discount1 ?? 0) - (terms.discount2 ?? 0)
    + (terms.additionalSale1 ?? 0) + (terms.additionalSale2 ?? 0)
    - (terms.trade ?? 0)
    + lateFees
    - earlyDiscount;
}
```

## File Organization
```
convex/
  schema.ts
  contacts/
    queries.ts        # All contact queries
    mutations.ts      # All contact mutations
  purchases/
    queries.ts
    mutations.ts
    helpers.ts        # Shared billing computation helpers
  billing/
    queries.ts        # Billing view queries (cash flow, this month, etc.)
